    "body": "5. We could also say that in such cases the mapping of empty string to null does not happen. I.e., we would preserve `#` or `?` in the serialized URL.\r\n6. We percent-encode the final code point of the path or query as needed.\r\n\r\nI think I like these a bit better than 2. 4 would be problematic for fragment navigation, which is definitely a thing in `data:` URLs. 3 seems a little surprising. Agreed on 1.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
