    "updated_at": "2021-09-28T00:41:04Z",
    "body": "I think I prefer 2 over 5. With 2, users have more options: if they want to keep the space and the delimiter, then they can explicitly opt into it by setting `.hash = '#'`. With 5, there's no way to remove the `#` through setters alone.\r\n\r\n6 seems a little surprising – we never only percent-encode one character. Chrome is also already running into some trouble trying to percent-encode more characters in non-special URLs (https://crbug.com/1252739), so ideally I'd like to keep the path the way it is.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
