    "updated_at": "2021-09-28T01:18:57Z",
    "body": "7. Start percent-encoding spaces in the paths of cannot-be-a-base URLs\r\n\r\nI can't think of anywhere else where naked spaces are allowed (not in the scheme, query, fragment, userinfo, not in domains, not in opaque hostnames, etc) and RFC-3986 also doesn't allow them. Are there use-cases which absolutely depend on non-encoded spaces being preserved verbatim in CBAB URL paths?",
