    "body": "@karwa Escaping `\\` in non-special paths sounds like a reasonable idea, but I'm not sure about the web compatibility. Browsers are consistent in not escaping `\\`, even though RFC 3986 disallows `\\` in paths and several non-browser implementations (e.g., Go) do escape it.\r\n\r\nEither way it should probably be in a separate ticket. (Edit: created #675 to track this.)",
